Aim:-
b. Write a Program to implement various types of visualization in python.

Algorithm:-
1. Start
2. Import matplotlib.pyplot as plt
3. Create two lists:
    . names → student names
    . marks → corresponding marks
4. Bar Chart
    . Create a new figure
    . Plot bar chart using plt.bar(names, marks)
    . Add title, X-label, and Y-label
    . Display using plt.show()
5. Line Chart
    . Create a new figure
    . Plot line chart using plt.plot(names, marks)
    . Add marker, title, X-label, and Y-label
    . Display using plt.show()
6. Pie Chart
    . Create a new figure
    . Plot pie chart using plt.pie(marks, labels=names)
    . Add percentage (autopct) and title
    . Display using plt.show()
7. Stop

Code:-
import matplotlib.pyplot as plt

names = ["A", "B", "C", "D"]
marks = [80, 75, 90, 85]

# Bar Chart
plt.figure()
plt.bar(names, marks)
plt.title("Bar Chart - Student Marks")
plt.xlabel("Students")
plt.ylabel("Marks")
plt.show()

# Line Chart
plt.figure()
plt.plot(names, marks, marker='o')
plt.title("Line Chart - Student Marks")
plt.xlabel("Students")
plt.ylabel("Marks")
plt.show()

# Pie Chart
plt.figure()
plt.pie(marks, labels=names, autopct="%1.1f%%")
plt.title("Pie Chart - Marks Distribution")
plt.show()
